  "worked_solution": "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
